  "title": "Red Hat Security Advisory: java-21-ibm-semeru-certified-jdk security update",
  "description": "Red Hat has issued a critical security update for the IBM Semeru Runtime Certified Edition 21 runtime environment, addressing multiple vulnerabilities in the OpenJDK components. These fixes enhance security in areas such as TLS extensions, SASL authentication, HTTP handling, certificate validation, and various file and image processing functionalities. The update also distrusts certain intermediate CA certificates due to security concerns. The advisory covers Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10.0 and 10.2 Extended Update Support versions across multiple architectures.",
